Subject: [PATCH 4/4] map-check v2: read Gemini's probability map from the raw
 response text with a visitor (raw_entries), so a repeated key in the object
 stays two entries and fails the check as 'repeated' (serde_json's map keeps
 only the last; Zeki #4992); bare NaN/Infinity tokens are not JSON, so such a
 response is unreadable and the answer invalid (seeded random play), as any
 unreadable reply. Tests feed literal response bytes through the real decode
 path (literal_stub): a repeated key (rejected, choice played, no
 probabilities) and NaN, Infinity, -Infinity (invalid). map_audit.py reads the
 stored raw response text as key/value pairs and as strict JSON, with raw-text
 controls

(cherry picked from commit 38024d6a6becfe13eaac3001b913eda6481582d9 onto pinned-late-reax 0e66836 for the Gemini Decision 1 repeat) Applied without conflict; the raw-entries test's DecisionClient literal gains budget: None.
